# Postgres
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/crm?schema=public"

# A direct, unpooled connection to that same database, used by
# `prisma migrate deploy` when the API is built on Vercel. Set it only if
# DATABASE_URL points at a pooler; POSTGRES_URL_NON_POOLING is read as a
# fallback. Locally there is nothing to set.
# DIRECT_DATABASE_URL=""

# A throwaway database for `bun run test`. The suite will not touch DATABASE_URL
# and refuses to run without this — these are real integration tests, they write
# and delete rows, and the pre-push hook runs them. The name has to end in
# `_test`. `bun run db:test` creates it and applies the migrations.
TEST_DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/crm_test?schema=public"

# One run of the suite, one database. `bun run test` mints an id when this is
# unset, creates `crm_<id>_test` next to TEST_DATABASE_URL, runs on it and drops
# it, so two runs on one machine never share rows. Set it only to run a single
# spec by hand: `TEST_RUN_ID=me bun run db:test` builds `crm_me_test`, and every
# `bun test` started with the same value lands there. Letters and digits only.
# TEST_RUN_ID=""

# PHIEN_DO — set by scripts/lan-do/phien-do.mjs inside a measure session to the name
# of that session's database (crm_<tree>_do), never by hand. PHIEN_DO_TEN_CAY
# overrides the tree name a session is keyed on; leave it unset outside tests.
# PHIEN_DO=""
# PHIEN_DO_TEN_CAY=""

# Test-only. The listing ingest spec reads the batch the crawler emitted from
# this path, relative to the repo root. Unset, it reads the batch signed into
# `_acceptance/tiep-thi-tuyen-doi-tac/evidence/`. A re-run of the crawler writes
# under `.acceptance-runs/` and points here, so it never rewrites signed evidence.
# LISTING_FIXTURE_BATCH=""

# Generate your own:  openssl rand -base64 32
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=""

# Who may sign in FIRST, on a brand-new install. This is a seed, not the
# authorisation model: it has a say only while the allow list is empty AND
# nobody has ever signed in. Once one person is in, the allow list on
# Settings -> Members is the only thing that decides, and this variable goes
# quiet. It no longer feeds the staff email domain either — that is a field in
# settings now.
#
# Comma-separated, and each entry is either a whole email domain or a single
# address:
#
#   ALLOWED_SIGN_IN="acme.com"                       everyone at your company
#   ALLOWED_SIGN_IN="acme.com,contractor@gmail.com"  …plus one outsider
#   ALLOWED_SIGN_IN="you@gmail.com"                  a one-person install
#
# Subdomains count, so "acme.com" also admits "you@mail.acme.com".
ALLOWED_SIGN_IN=""

# Google is the sign-in method a clone starts with, and the same client is what
# reads Gmail and Calendar. Set both or neither — half a pair is a sign-in
# button that fails at Google.
#
# Leave them empty only if you sign in with Microsoft below, or with your own
# identity provider added on Settings → SSO. With none of the three there is no
# way in at all, and the sign-in page says as much rather than showing you
# nothing.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=""
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=""

# Google Sheets — tài khoản dịch vụ chỉ đọc cho KR nguồn Google Sheets (lượt 6 OKR).
# Email của tài khoản dịch vụ; người dùng chia sẻ bảng tính cho địa chỉ này. Vắng thì nguồn Sheets ẩn.
GOOGLE_SHEETS_EMAIL=""
# Khoá riêng PEM của tài khoản đó (\n viết thành \\n). API chỉ xem khoá đã đặt chưa và đọc email; tác tử dùng khoá để đọc bảng.
GOOGLE_SHEETS_KHOA=""
# Tuỳ chọn, chỉ cho phiên đo trỏ tới Google giả. Vắng là máy chủ thật của Google
# (oauth2.googleapis.com/token và sheets.googleapis.com/v4/spreadsheets). Chỉ tác tử đọc,
# và chỉ khi NODE_ENV khác "production" — bản chạy thật luôn gọi Google thật.
# OKR_SHEETS_TOKEN_URL=""
# OKR_SHEETS_API_URL=""

# Microsoft 365 / Entra ID — the other sign-in method, and the same app
# registration is what reads Outlook mail. Set both or neither, exactly like
# the Google pair.
#
# Create the app at https://portal.azure.com → Microsoft Entra ID → App
# registrations, add the redirect URI <API_URL>/api/auth/callback/microsoft,
# and give it the delegated Graph permissions User.Read and Mail.Read. The
# README has the full walkthrough.
#
# You can set Google and Microsoft together: the sign-in page offers both, and
# a rep's mail is read from whichever they signed in with.
# MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID=""
# MICROSOFT_CLIENT_SECRET=""

# Optional. Enables Slack account linking on Settings > Connections.
# Add APP_URL + /api/auth/oauth2/callback/slack as the Slack OAuth redirect URL.
# SLACK_CLIENT_ID=""
# SLACK_CLIENT_SECRET=""

# Optional fallback for the morning reminder on Zalo and the bot that answers link codes.
# Normally an admin pastes the Bot Token on Settings › Connections › Zalo; it is stored
# in AppSetting and wins over ZALO_BOT_TOKEN.
# Create the bot in the Zalo app: open the official account «Zalo Bot Manager» and tap Create bot.
# The Bot Token looks like 123456:abc…, not the webhook Secret Token. Only apps/agent reads it.
# ZALO_BOT_TOKEN=""
# Optional fallback. Secret Zalo sends in X-Bot-Api-Secret-Token with every webhook call; 8–256 characters.
# When the bot is switched on from the screen the agent generates one and keeps it in AppSetting,
# which wins over ZALO_WEBHOOK_SECRET. Register a fallback with
# `bun run --filter=agent zalo:webhook https://<agent>/zalo/webhook`. Only apps/agent reads it.
# ZALO_WEBHOOK_SECRET=""
# Optional. Base URL of the Zalo Bot API; empty means https://bot-api.zaloplatforms.com.
# Set it only to run against a fake Zalo in tests. Only apps/agent reads it.
# ZALO_API_URL=""
# Measurement only — leave empty in production. "1" turns off the tro_ly_okr stand-in
# that non-OKR sessions see, so a measurement run can watch the root call the real
# OKR subagent (the replay case). Read only when NODE_ENV is not production.
# Only apps/agent reads it.
# TRO_LY_OKR_BO_DE=""

# Which Entra tenant may sign in. "common" (the default) accepts any work,
# school or personal Microsoft account and leans on ALLOWED_SIGN_IN to decide
# who actually gets in; your own tenant's GUID refuses everyone else at
# Microsoft, before they ever reach us. "organizations" allows any work or
# school account but no personal ones.
# MICROSOFT_TENANT_ID="common"

# Serve the landing page at "/". It markets *this* product, so it is off unless
# you say otherwise: on an install of your own, a stranger arriving at the root
# is sent to /sign-in instead. The only value that turns it on is "true".
# IS_MARKETING="true"


# ── Where things are ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only needed when you deploy. The defaults below are the localhost ones.

# The API. Also the origin that mints session cookies and serves /api/auth/*.
# API_URL="http://localhost:3001"

# The web app. Comma-separate if it is served from more than one origin —
# the first is canonical, and the rest are simply allowed to call the API.
# The agent reads the first one too, to put an "open the plan" link on each
# line of the morning reminder it sends on Slack. Unset, the reminder is still
# sent, just without links.
# APP_URL="http://localhost:3000"

# Only when the API and the app are on different subdomains of one parent,
# e.g. api.example.com and app.example.com — then set ".example.com" so one
# session cookie covers both.
# AUTH_COOKIE_DOMAIN=""

# The research agent, which is its own deployment. The API reads this too, to
# tell the agent a logo or a photograph is waiting rather than letting it find
# out on its next minute.
# AGENT_URL="http://127.0.0.1:2000"

# Port used by the self-hosted Eve service. Hosted runtimes can keep injecting
# their standard PORT variable instead.
# AGENT_PORT="2000"

# Lets a signed-in rep talk to the agent from the contact sheet.
#
# The browser never calls the agent directly. The app proxies /eve/v1/* on its
# own origin, checks the session, and mints a two-minute token signed with this
# secret; the agent verifies it and learns *which rep* is asking. Set the same
# value for both processes.  openssl rand -base64 32
#
# It also authorises two calls the API makes to the agent: the dispatch poke,
# which is what makes a new company's logo appear as it is added instead of on
# the next minute's tick, and the check that a Context API key is real before
# it is saved.
#
# Leave it unset and the Agent tab reports that it is not configured, the poke
# is skipped rather than sent unauthenticated, and a Context key is saved
# without being checked. Nothing else changes: the agent still runs on its own
# schedule.
# AGENT_BRIDGE_SECRET=""

# The OKR drafting assistant is a second eve deployment (apps/agent-okr) with
# one tool and no partner data. The app forwards /eve/agents/okr/eve/v1/* to it.
# The default is the port `eve dev --port 2100` in apps/agent-okr listens on;
# 127.0.0.1, not localhost, for the same IPv4 reason as AGENT_URL. The API never
# reads this variable, so it is not in env.validation.ts.
# OKR_AGENT_URL="http://127.0.0.1:2100"

# Signs the two-minute token the OKR gate mints (audience crm-okr-agent). A
# different secret from AGENT_BRIDGE_SECRET on purpose: a token for one agent
# must not open the other. Set the same value for apps/app and apps/agent-okr.
# Unset, the OKR drafting screen reports that it is not configured (503).
# openssl rand -base64 32
# OKR_AGENT_BRIDGE_SECRET=""

# PORT="3001"


# ── Optional: what the agent can do ──────────────────────────────────────────
# The research agent works with none of these — it falls back to what the CRM
# already knows (your own email and calendar history) and simply reports what
# it could not check. Each key you add unlocks one more place it can look, and
# it tells you at startup which ones are on.

# Perplexity — finds where a person lives on the web, and recent news worth
# knowing before a call. https://perplexity.ai/settings/api
# PERPLEXITY_API_KEY=""

# GitHub — raises the rate limit when matching contacts to GitHub profiles.
# Any classic token with no scopes will do.
# GITHUB_TOKEN=""

# Bản chụp lộ trình — không phải biến của app. Đặt làm bí mật GitHub Actions của kho
# (Settings › Secrets and variables › Actions) cho workflow ban-chup-lo-trinh.yml: khoá loại
# «Đẩy lộ trình» tạo ở Cài đặt › Khoá API bởi chủ hoặc quản trị. Vắng thì lượt đẩy bỏ qua
# (ghi chú «chua-cai») và trang Lộ trình đọc lộ trình đóng sẵn trong bản dựng.
# CRM_KHOA_DAY_LO_TRINH=""

# Vercel Blob — where every logo and profile picture in the CRM is kept.
#
# The URLs these arrive on are somebody else's: LinkedIn signs theirs with an
# expiry a few weeks out, a brand CDN is a rate limit on a page that draws forty
# logos, and a company's own favicon is served by a company with no idea we are
# drawing it. So the bytes are copied once and the record points at our copy.
#
# Read by the agent, by the API — which writes a favicon and a signed-in user's
# Google avatar — and by the seed. Not by the Next.js app, which only needs to
# recognise one of our URLs to route it through the image optimizer.
#
# Without it, a contact's photograph is not stored at all, because a URL that
# works today and 404s next month is worse than initials and nobody can tell
# which it will be. Everything else — logos, favicons, avatars — keeps the
# origin's URL and renders as an ordinary hotlinked image.
#
# This store is PUBLIC. The document library keeps its files in a separate
# private store — see KHO_TAI_LIEU_BLOB_TOKEN below.
# BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=""

# Vercel Blob — the Word and PDF sources people upload to the document library
# (Kho tài liệu), in their own PRIVATE store, apart from the public one above.
# One store is either public or private, so the two cannot share a token.
#
# Paste the private store's read-write token here. Keep that store not
# connected to any Vercel project (không gắn dự án): connecting it makes Vercel
# set BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN to this private token, and logos would then be
# written into the private store.
#
# Read by the API, which signs uploads and downloads, and by the agent, which
# reads a source back to draft a page. There is no fallback to
# BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN: without this, «Tải nguồn lên» stays locked and nothing
# throws.
# KHO_TAI_LIEU_BLOB_TOKEN=""

# The model the agent runs on is reached through the Vercel AI Gateway. On
# Vercel this is handled by OIDC and needs nothing; elsewhere, set a key.
# Which model is a setting, not a variable — change it on the settings page.
# https://vercel.com/docs/ai-gateway
# AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY=""

# A second AI Gateway key used only by the document library: the machine that
# drafts pages from uploaded Word and PDF files, and the AI assistant that
# answers questions from approved pages. Their spend shows apart on the Gateway.
# Without it both use the key above; nothing else changes.
# KHO_TAI_LIEU_AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY=""

# A third AI Gateway key used only by Trợ lý OKR (suggestions and weekly
# summaries), so its spend is billed apart and the key can carry its own monthly
# budget. Without it Trợ lý OKR runs on AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY, or on Vercel OIDC.
# OKR_AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY=""


# ── Optional: operations ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Shared cache. Without it each instance caches in its own memory, which is
# correct — just not shared. Recommended in production once website tracking is
# on: the compiled tracking config, the collector's rate limit and the hourly
# cap on contacts created from forms are all counted here, and per-instance
# counters let a multi-instance deployment exceed both.
# REDIS_URL="redis://localhost:6379"
# CACHE_TTL_MS="60000"

# Bearer token guarding POST /internal/sync/google, the Gmail/Calendar cron
# route, and POST /internal/tracking/retention, the nightly sweep that deletes
# tracked page views older than 90 days. Both refuse to run without it. At
# least 16 characters.
# CRON_SECRET=""

# Log every SQL statement Prisma runs, at debug level, without bound
# parameters. Off by default: it buries every other line under a wall of
# SELECTs.
# PRISMA_LOG_QUERIES="true"


# ── Listing ingest ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Bearer token guarding POST /internal/listings/ingest, the endpoint the
# listing crawler in tools/listing-crawl posts batches to. Without it the
# endpoint refuses with 503 and no listing data can enter the CRM. At least 16
# characters.
# LISTING_INGEST_SECRET=""

# Khoa Bearer cho diem nhan so lieu tu nen tang OneHub (POST /internal/onboarding/ingest).
# Chua khai thi diem nhan tra 503 va moi thu khac van chay — mat mot nang luc, khong sap module.
# ONEHUB_PLATFORM_INGEST_SECRET=""


# ── Anonymous usage telemetry ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This repo is MIT and cloned rather than installed, so there is no download
# count and no runtime signal. Once a day the API sends one event of counts —
# how many contacts exist in bands rather than exactly, which of the agent's
# tools were called, how the evidence ledger behaved, which optional keys are
# set as booleans — tied to a random UUID generated by the first migration.
#
# It is server-side only. There is no posthog-js anywhere, no autocapture and
# no session replay, because autocapture on a CRM would lift contact names and
# deal amounts out of your database. No name, address, company, subject line,
# amount, prompt or key is ever sent, and neither is your IP: every event
# carries $ip: null with geoip off.
#
# docs/telemetry.md names every event and every property that is sent, and
# lists what never is.

# Turn it off. "1" is the whole interface, and DO_NOT_TRACK=1 does the same.
# When either is set no client is created, so nothing can be sent later.
#
# There is no variable for where it goes: the project key and host are written
# into packages/telemetry, because a write-only key is not a secret and a
# variable would only suggest it were one. Change them there if you want the
# numbers in your own project.
# CRM_TELEMETRY_DISABLED="1"

# Chỉ dành cho bộ kiểm của apps/agent-okr. Hai bộ bài dựng eve dev thật
# (app-rieng, hong-chen) tự bỏ qua kèm một dòng thông báo khi Node trên máy
# dưới 24, vì eve đòi Node 24. Đặt "1" thì bỏ qua thành lỗi: job «tác nhân OKR
# trên Node 24» của acceptance.yml đặt biến này để không bao giờ xanh khi hai
# bộ bài chưa chạy. Máy dev không cần đặt.
# CRM_EVE_BAT_BUOC="1"

# Mở nhánh /proto — phòng trưng bày giao diện chạy được, dùng cho nghi thức
# design-pass trước Cổng 1. Đặt đúng chuỗi "1" mới mở; mọi giá trị khác, kể cả
# "0", "false" và "true", đều giữ nhánh ở trạng thái không tồn tại (404). Cờ đọc
# ở proxy LÚC CHẠY, nên bật hay tắt không cần dựng lại. Chỉ apps/app đọc biến
# này, API không đọc, nên nó KHÔNG khai trong
# apps/api/src/config/env.validation.ts — nhưng nó PHẢI có trong
# globalPassThroughEnv của turbo.json ở gốc, nhà thứ ba mà docs/environment.md
# gọi là "cái hay cắn": thiếu nó thì turbo lọc biến khỏi mọi task và lệnh dev
# một dòng sẽ im lặng không mở được proto. Bản chạy thật không đặt nó.
# PROTO_ROUTE="1"

# Đổi thư mục Next dựng vào, cho apps/app. Chỉ dùng cho phép đo: răng nghiệm thu
# dựng vào một thư mục riêng để không tranh khoá với lệnh cổng chung — Next khoá
# theo THƯ MỤC DỰNG chứ không theo cổng, nên đây là cách duy nhất chạy hai bản
# dựng hay hai máy chủ cùng lúc. Bản chạy thật và người dùng thường KHÔNG đặt nó;
# để trống thì Next dùng ".next" như mặc định. Cố ý KHÔNG khai vào
# globalPassThroughEnv của turbo.json: turbo khai outputs là ".next/**", nên cho
# biến này đi qua turbo sẽ làm cache trỏ vào một thư mục không phải thư mục vừa
# sinh ra.
# PROTO_DIST_DIR=".next-proto-do"

# Khoá license ReUI, chỉ dùng lúc CÀI thành phần vào packages/ui bằng
# `bun run ui:add @reui/<tên>` — không app nào đọc nó lúc chạy, nên nó không có
# trong env.validation.ts hay turbo.json. Block trả phí cần khoá thật (gói Pro);
# thành phần và ví dụ c-* miễn phí chỉ cần một chuỗi khác rỗng, vì CLI shadcn từ
# chối mọi mục @reui khi biến này trống. Quy ước dùng ReUI: docs/reui.md.
# REUI_LICENSE_KEY=""

# Chỉ cho bài kiểm. Đặt "1" khi chạy apps/api/test/deals-board.spec.ts thì bài
# kiểm ghi đầu ra thật của deals.board vào apps/app/test/fixtures/ — dữ liệu mà
# bài kiểm màn bảng cột đọc lại. Để trống thì không ghi gì, nên bun run test
# thường ngày không làm bẩn cây. Ghi lại khi hình dạng đầu ra của deals.board đổi.
# GHI_FIXTURE_BANG_COT="1"

# Gửi thư ra ngoài — hiện chỉ dùng cho liên kết đặt lại mật khẩu ở /quen-mat-khau
# và thư báo sau khi mật khẩu bị đổi. Khai cả hai hoặc không khai cái nào:
# packages/auth/src/env.ts ném lỗi nếu chỉ có một. Không khai thì cửa quên mật
# khẩu tự ẩn, người dùng vẫn xin liên kết qua quản trị như trước.
# Khoá lấy ở resend.com; MAIL_FROM phải là địa chỉ thuộc tên miền đã xác minh
# SPF/DKIM ở đó, nếu không thư sẽ vào hộp rác hoặc bị chặn thẳng.
#   RESEND_API_KEY="re_..."
#   MAIL_FROM="OneHub Center <no-reply@onehub.center>"
# RESEND_API_KEY=""
# MAIL_FROM=""

# Signals — read by `scripts/tin-hieu/keo-ve.ts` and `scripts/tin-hieu/lich.ts`, never by
# the API. CRM_API_URL is the API's public origin. CRM_KHOA_KEO_TIN_HIEU is a
# "signals only" key (Settings › API keys › Key for: Only pulling signals into the repo,
# owner/admin only): it can call the scheduled pull route and nothing else — it never
# signs in. The daily schedule (.github/workflows/tin-hieu-keo-ve.yml) reads it and
# CRM_API_URL from the repo's Actions secrets. CRM_API_KEY is an owner/admin full key,
# kept for a manual pull on the owner's machine; when both are set the signals-only key
# wins. Missing the URL or both keys: the command exits 2 and writes nothing.
# CRM_API_URL=""
# CRM_KHOA_KEO_TIN_HIEU=""
# CRM_API_KEY=""
